{"name":"Sunbeam","hex":"#f5edb2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sunbeam","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An unincorporated community in Moffat County, Colorado, United States.","An unincorporated community in Mercer County, Illinois, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sunbeam"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sunbeam","blocks":[{"text":"A sunbeam, in meteorological optics, is a beam of sunlight that appears to radiate from the position of the Sun. Shining through openings in clouds or between other objects such as mountains and buildings, these beams of particle-scattered sunlight are essentially parallel shafts separated by darker shadowed volumes. Their apparent convergence in the sky is a visual illusion from linear perspective. The same illusion causes the apparent convergence of parallel lines on a long straight road or hallway at a distant vanishing point. The scattering particles that make sunlight visible may be air molecules or particulates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Crepuscular_Rays_Reno_Nevada_USA.jpg/330px-Crepuscular_Rays_Reno_Nevada_USA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunbeam","wikidata":"Q111660583"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Crepuscular_Rays%2C_India.JPG/500px-Crepuscular_Rays%2C_India.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Crepuscular_Rays%2C_India.JPG/1280px-Crepuscular_Rays%2C_India.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Crepuscular_Rays%2C_India.JPG/500px-Crepuscular_Rays%2C_India.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Daytime sunbeams as seen from the ISS, illustrating their parallel nature","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrepuscular_Rays%2C_India.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Taipei_crepuscular_rays_%E8%87%BA%E5%8C%97%E9%9B%B2%E9%9A%99%E5%85%89_2018.jpg/500px-Taipei_crepuscular_rays_%E8%87%BA%E5%8C%97%E9%9B%B2%E9%9A%99%E5%85%89_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Taipei_crepuscular_rays_%E8%87%BA%E5%8C%97%E9%9B%B2%E9%9A%99%E5%85%89_2018.jpg/1280px-Taipei_crepuscular_rays_%E8%87%BA%E5%8C%97%E9%9B%B2%E9%9A%99%E5%85%89_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Taipei_crepuscular_rays_%E8%87%BA%E5%8C%97%E9%9B%B2%E9%9A%99%E5%85%89_2018.jpg/500px-Taipei_crepuscular_rays_%E8%87%BA%E5%8C%97%E9%9B%B2%E9%9A%99%E5%85%89_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Crepuscular rays as seen from Taipei, Taiwan (2018)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATaipei_crepuscular_rays_%E8%87%BA%E5%8C%97%E9%9B%B2%E9%9A%99%E5%85%89_2018.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Anticrepuscular_rays_from_above.jpg/500px-Anticrepuscular_rays_from_above.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Anticrepuscular_rays_from_above.jpg/500px-Anticrepuscular_rays_from_above.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"These anticrepuscular rays appear to converge at the antisolar point, as viewed from an aircraft above the clouded ocean.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnticrepuscular_rays_from_above.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Renaissance_Square_in_Stepanakert.jpg/500px-Renaissance_Square_in_Stepanakert.jpg?utm_source=en.wiki